From f4c70ab7c5e70a853684242223a4e2a7817fe728 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:08:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(app,ui): mod vises - fixed and adjustable jaw blocks
 on the plate grid

A plate-mounted modular vise is two jaw-block fixtures bolted to a
fixture plate's grid (#819): a fixed block on a named hole, and an
adjustable block on the nearest hole clear of the stock, slid along its
slots until its face touches the stock. One undoable PlaceModVisePair
places both as riders of the plate (moving it carries them, deleting it
lets go of them); each is a meshed fixture judged by the existing
fixture laws. Refusals by name: out of the slots' reach, off the plate,
no grid, no stock, stock in the fixed jaw or beside the jaws, bolts
between holes, an off-quarter turn, nonsense figures.

Generic presets of our own (1 in 3/8-16, 2 in 1/2-13, 50 mm M12 grids);
an optional, leniently read `mod_jaw` key in the project file; MCP
add_mod_vise_pair; "Add mod vise pair..." on a plate's Fixtures row.
Dual-station blocks and edit/re-fit are split off to #832.

Fixes #820

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
